{"id":12952897,"tag_name":"release_1.1","target_commitish":"master","name":"OpenRGB Release 1.1","body":"This is a bugfix release meant to address several issues found in the 1.0 release.\r\n\r\n* Fix an issue with the \"Do not show again\" checkbox not saving\r\n* Fix an issue with the OpenRGB SDK server not replying to the plugin list request in headless mode\r\n* Fix an issue with the OpenRGB SDK server device indices on protocol versions \u003c 6\r\n* Fix several issues with the command line interface regarding resizing, profile loading, and applying settings to devices\r\n* Device-specific improvements on several device controllers to improve hotplug behavior and fix potential deadlocks\r\n\r\nOn Windows, you will need to install https://pawnio.eu for OpenRGB to access RAM, older motherboards, and certain other devices.  You must also run as Administrator or install with the background service option for PawnIO to be able to access these devices.\r\n\r\nOn Linux, if you use the .deb or .rpm packages, they depend on a fork of hidapi called hidapi-hotplug.  You can download the hidapi-hotplug packages from here:\r\n\r\nhttps://codeberg.org/OpenRGB/hidapi-hotplug/releases/tag/hidapi-hotplug-0.15.0","url":"https://codeberg.org/api/v1/repos/OpenRGB/OpenRGB/releases/12952897","html_url":"https://codeberg.org/OpenRGB/OpenRGB/releases/tag/release_1.1","tarball_url":"https://codeberg.org/OpenRGB/OpenRGB/archive/release_1.1.tar.gz","zipball_url":"https://codeberg.org/OpenRGB/OpenRGB/archive/release_1.1.zip","hide_archive_links":false,"upload_url":"https://codeberg.org/api/v1/repos/OpenRGB/OpenRGB/releases/12952897/assets","draft":false,"prerelease":false,"created_at":"2026-10-16T23:37:19+02:00","published_at":"2026-10-16T23:37:19+02:00","author":{"id":113023,"login":"CalcProgrammer1","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"Adam Honse","email":"calcprogrammer1@noreply.codeberg.org","avatar_url":"https://codeberg.org/avatars/3c68e290e8707bdd41b2b50ab3e0fffb3ed9e83c866b9